clang / llvm-mingw build fixes (phase 4: portable toolchain + PGO); GS state compared field by field.
- GS draw state (gs_types.h): every register struct of GSDrawState gets a defaulted operator==, and the two raw memcmp
  compares (hw backend sameState, threaded backend draw-state dedup) use it. The structs have padding bytes the language
  leaves unspecified; MSVC happened to keep them equal, clang does not, so with clang no two states compared equal: every
  primitive became its own batch and its own queued state (GS thread ~5.5 s busy per 5 s, ~2 fps in 3D).
- hw backend draw(): the shadow-volume counting passes (COLCLAMP=0, ALPHA Cs*FIX+Cd, flat colour G += 255 then G += 1) share
  one GS state, so with the field-wise compare one batch holds both colours; the fixed-function wrap needs one colour per
  draw, otherwise each triangle goes through the shader blend with a texture barrier in between (SwapBuffers blocked ~1 s
  per frame in fights). Such a batch is drawn as consecutive runs of one colour, in order.
- VUops.cpp: <cstdlib> for std::getenv (MSVC included it indirectly). ps2_vu1_native.inl: the slot-count static_assert
  uses std::extent_v (clang rejects std::size on a reference in a constant expression).
- ps2_runtime.cpp: an instrumented clang build (-fprofile-instr-generate) writes its profile when the window is closed
  (weak reference to __llvm_profile_write_file; the shutdown after it can wait on worker threads and never reach the
  profile runtime's exit hook). No effect on other builds.
Measured on the ship with the launcher's defaults, combat t=70-145 s, same day: MSVC 58.0 avg / 53.1 min fps;
llvm-mingw 20261020 (clang 23.1.4, -O3 -march=native, static) 55.6 / 50.4; same + PGO trained on this scripted run
59.4 / 57.9 (EE thread -27 %, GS -21 %, VU1 worker +8 % against MSVC). Full build ~15 min with clang, 45-60 min with MSVC.

